-- title:
--   End of blown-up supersingular chart labels an Igusa prime
-- statement:
--   Throughout write $C := \mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of those elements of $K$ that are integral over $A[j]$, and $X := \mathtt{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ for the scheme obtained as the pushout of the two morphisms $\mathtt{fFin} : \mathtt{XMid} \to \operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\mathtt{fInf} : \mathtt{XMid} \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{chartAlgInf}\,A\,K\,j)$, with structure morphism $\mathtt{toBase} : X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ and with $\mathtt{ιFin} : \operatorname{Spec} C \to X$ the corresponding leg of the pushout.
--
--   **Level data.** A prime $q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$ are fixed. $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is, by `hH₁`, the intersection of $\mathtt{levelH}\,q\,M'$ — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. The intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L((t))$ is, by `hK`, the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   **Base ring and chart.** $A$ is a Henselian discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with the $L$-structure. The element $j \in K$ has, by `hj`, Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of $\mathtt{jq}$ (the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function), and $j \neq 0$. Further, $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **Supersingular point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, and `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathtt{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, the set of $x \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $x$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The hypothesis `hArig` (an existence statement with seven clauses, summarised here).** For every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the pullback of $\varpi$ along $\mathtt{toBase}$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $\mathtt{ιFin}(y') = z$ at which the same supersingularity condition as in `hss` holds for $y'$, there exist: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ carrying $\varpi$ to a generator of $\mathfrak{m}_W$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$, $v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v - fu\big)$, subject to: $e$ carries the germ of a constant $a \in A$ to the class of $\sigma(a)$; every automorphism $\tau$ of $K/L$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of $\mathtt{IsLevelAutAt}\,L\,q\,\zeta\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1$ (matching, after the embedding $\iota$, the slash action of $\mathtt{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ on quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$), for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, preserves $C$; such $\tau$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ act trivially on $C/y'$; every such $\tau$ acting trivially on $C/y'$ is realised through $e$ by a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ fixing the constants $W$ and sending $X_{j}$, modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, to $\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ for a matrix $M$ over $W$ with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij} \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$, with $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ containing $\sigma(\varpi)$, not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$, and containing linear forms $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1$ up to terms in $(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk; for such a prime with tangent form $X_0$, an element $a \in C$ has germ in the contraction of the prime exactly when every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and finally $\mathtt{jqNModC}\,L\,q$ (the $j$-series in $\mathsf{q}^q$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, is congruent modulo $y'$ to some $a_0 \in A$, and the germ of $\mathtt{jqNModC}\,L\,q - a_0$ corresponds under $e$ to the class of a power series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0 \geq 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ leading form takes unit values at all pairs $(a,b)$ in $W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   **A fixed chart presentation.** Data $z$, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $\mathtt{ιFin}(y') = z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y'$ the prime $y$ (`hy'y`), are fixed, together with $W_1$, $\sigma_1$, $f_1, u_1, v_1$ and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ with $S_1 := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1 - f_1u_1)$ of exactly the above shape; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this datum precisely the seven clauses just listed.
--
--   **The centre and the blow-up charts.** The ideal $J$ of $C$ is, by `hJ`, the infimum (intersection) of the ideals $(\tau|_C)^{-1}\big((e_1 \circ \text{completion} \circ \text{germ})^{-1}(\sigma_1\varpi_t, X_0, X_1)\big)$ taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. The subalgebra $B$ is, by `hB`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained from the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, that is the affine blow-up chart $C[J/\varpi_t]$.
--
--   **The distinguished valuation ring.** $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hR1` (two clauses) states $C \subseteq B$ and that $K$ is the field of fractions of $B$; `hR2` (three clauses) states that $B$ is formally smooth over $A$, of finite presentation over $A$, and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that $W$ meets $L$ exactly in the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if the image of $b$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$.
--
--   **The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses).** First, for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to \mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\,q\,k_A$ whose zero set is exactly the set of elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, which is compatible with the residue map on $A$, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ there are a unit $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in $\mathtt{hSubgroup}\,q$ (the kernel of $(g,c) \mapsto \det g \cdot c^{q+1}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q) \times \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$) such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathtt{hAction}\,q\,k_A$ of that element applied to $\rho$, and $c \neq 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$. Second, $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. Third, every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$ arises from some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense that $\tau$ maps every $b \in B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ into $B$ and into $Q$. Fourth, if $b \in B$ is such that $\tau(b) \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ for all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\tau(b) \in B$, then the image of $\varpi$ divides $b$ in $B$. Fifth, a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **The end $O$.** $O$ is a subring of $K$ for which `hO` asserts: there is $a \in J$ with non-zero image in $K$ such that, $B_a$ denoting the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained from the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : xa \in J\}$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, with no element of $y$ becoming a unit in $O$, and with $B \not\subseteq O$. Moreover $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ is local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), and $C \subseteq O$ (`hCO`).
--
--   **The stability hypothesis `hIgStab`.** Every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ which meets $L$ exactly in the image of $A$, whose maximal ideal contains the image of $\varpi$, which contains $C$, and for which some $c \in C$ has the property that $p(c)$ lies in $V \setminus \mathfrak{m}_V$ for every monic $p \in A[T]$, is stable under every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exists a prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$ with $\mathfrak{p} \subseteq y$ and $\mathfrak{p} \neq y$, such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with the properties that the image of $x \in L$ lies in $V$ exactly when $x$ lies in the image of $A$, and that the image of $\varpi$, if it lies in $V$, lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, the following holds whenever $j \in V$ and $p(j) \notin \mathfrak{m}_V$ for every monic $p \in A[T]$ with $p(j) \in V$:
--
--   (1) if $O \subseteq V$, then for every $b \in C$ whose image lies in $V$, that image lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{p}$;
--
--   (2) if some $f \in O$ does not lie in $V$, then there exists a prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}'$ of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, with $\mathfrak{p}' \subseteq y$, $\mathfrak{p}' \neq y$ and $\mathfrak{p}' \neq \mathfrak{p}$, such that for every $b \in C$ whose image lies in $V$, that image lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{p}'$.
--
--   Thus a single prime $\mathfrak{p}$, strictly below the supersingular point $y$, is attached to the end $O$ of the blow-up, and the valuation rings of the stated Igusa type are sorted by whether they dominate $O$ or not.
--
--   This is a step in the analysis of the reduction at $q$ of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ in the diamond frame in which the auxiliary full level is replaced by a congruence condition modulo a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$: an end of the blow-up of the supersingular chart along the equivariant centre $J$ singles out one prime of the chart algebra below the supersingular point, and the Igusa-type valuation subrings of $K$ are classified by it. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_labelUnit_chartAlgFin_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_labelUnit_chartAlgFin_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd).
